From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: k114s-integration <integration@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:51:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/93] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: optional panel
 brightness floor

A panel node may carry apple,min-brightness: the lowest level, in the
unit of apple,max-brightness, that a brightness request can reach where
the firmware takes the level in nits. Turning the display off is not
affected.

K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro) integration patch, not from
upstream. Nobody has reported a brightness write on a K-board OLED
panel, and what such a panel shows at 0 nits is not known, so the K114s
tree names a floor.

Hardware-untested: not booted on any machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index 193ceda4642..171c49cd125 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -514,6 +514,14 @@ properties:
       apple,max-brightness:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
         description: Maximum firmware backlight level.
+      apple,min-brightness:
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        description:
+          Lowest level a brightness request can reach, in the unit of
+          apple,max-brightness and below it, where the firmware takes the
+          level in nits. A lower request, zero included, is raised to this
+          level. Turning the display off (DPMS, blanking, suspend) is not
+          affected.
     required:
       - compatible
     additionalProperties: false
